<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lake Petén Itzá</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lake <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peten">Petén</a> Itzá is a lake in the Petén lowlands of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guatemala">Guatemala</a> and the setting of several Maya polities. Motul de San José, seat of the Classic Ik' kingdom, stood on its northern side, and in the Postclassic the Itza capital Nojpetén occupied an island in the lake, with the Kowoj settled on its north-eastern shores. Nojpetén was the last independent Maya kingdom, falling to the Spanish in 1697.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lake-peten-itza.jpg" alt="Lake Petén Itzá" width="320" height="169" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: R. Villalobos · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Peten_Itza_lake.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
